# Security and caching headers for the static files (Cloudflare Pages).
# They do not reach the booking API: functions/_lib/http.ts sets its own.
#
# The CSP only stops the site being framed elsewhere, <base> hijacking and
# plugins. It deliberately does not limit scripts or connections: the
# assistant on /assistant loads from chatbot-dentisti.vercel.app and talks
# to its API on Railway, and that cannot be tested from a build machine.
# HSTS covers www (it redirects to the apex over HTTPS); no preload, which
# is hard to undo.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'

# Vite names every file here after its content, so a changed file is a new
# address: these can be kept for a year without asking again.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
